Phase 1 — Foundation
Supabase project setup

Database schema (users, buildings, floors, rooms, beds, decks, occupants, payments)

Row Level Security (RLS) — so each user only sees their own data

Phase 2 — Backend (FastAPI)
Project skeleton (main.py, config, database client)

Auth routes (signup, login, me)

Buildings routes (create with nested floors/rooms/beds/decks, list, update, delete)

Floors / Rooms / Beds / Decks routes (nested CRUD)

Occupants routes (assign to deck, check-in/out)

Payments routes (record, list, update status)

Phase 3 — Connect Frontend
Axios/fetch service layer

Wire Admin → backend (real save to DB)

Wire Header dropdown → backend (real buildings)

Wire Dashboard, Floors, Rooms, Occupants, Payments → backend

Add auth pages (Login / Signup) and protect routes

Phase 4 — Polish
Loading skeletons

Error handling & toasts

Form validation

Deployment (backend on Render/Fly, frontend on Vercel, DB on Supabase)

⚠️ Important Decisions Before We Start
Please confirm these 4 things so I don’t guess:

1. Backend framework
FastAPI (recommended — modern, async, great with Supabase)

Flask (simpler but older)

Django (heavier, has its own ORM — overkill here)

👉 My pick: FastAPI

2. Authentication
Supabase Auth (built-in, handles JWT, email, magic links, OAuth) — recommended

Custom JWT with FastAPI

👉 My pick: Supabase Auth — saves weeks of work

3. Database access from backend
Supabase Python client (supabase-py) — simplest, matches your choice

SQLAlchemy + psycopg — more control, more boilerplate

👉 My pick: supabase-py — clean and aligned with your DB choice

4. Local setup
Do you already have:

A Supabase account and project created? (Yes / No)

Python 3.10+ installed locally? (Yes / No)

Familiarity with running a Python server (uvicorn)? (Yes / No)